1
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Mythica: The Necromancer is a fantasy, action,
adventure film directed by A. Todd Smith.

2
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:30,000
The young wizard Marek is forced to lead her band of would-be heroes on a mission
for the corrupt Thieves Guild, which has taken her friend hostage.

3
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Their journey will take them straight into the wicked
clutches of Szorlok, their greatest enemy.

4
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Marek, played by Melanie Stone.

5
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Thane, played by Adam Johnson.

6
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Dagen, played by Jake Stormoen.

7
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:30,000
Teela, played by Nicola Posener.

8
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:42,000
Betylla, played by Philip Brodie.

9
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Szorlok, played by Matthew Mercer.

10
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Mythica is a series of primarily direct-to-video fantasy films.

11
01:08:12,000 --> 01:08:18,000
The films are produced by Arrowstorm Entertainment, with first film Mythica: A Quest for
Heroes being partly funded by a Kickstarter campaign that collected $94,294.

12
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
There are six films in the Mythica series, all produced and
co-written by Jason Faller and Kynan Griffin.

13
01:20:36,000 --> 01:20:42,000
The films star Melanie Stone as Marek, an escaped slave girl and budding magician, and co-star Kevin Sorbo as Gojun Pye the magician who trains
her, along with Adam Johnson, Jake Stormoen, and Nicola Posener as those that team up with Marek on various quests together.

14
01:26:48,000 --> 01:26:54,000
The film explores themes of magic, sword, sorcery, necromancer.
